segments.compiledPrompt:
[REFERENCE MATERIALS]
@classroom = a sunny kindergarten classroom, rug and carpet mats, banner reading MY FAMILY.
@location1 = the same classroom from the teacher's side, defining the camera side of the action.
@Mia = a five-year-old girl, huge bright eyes, yellow hair clip.
@Ben = a five-year-old boy, short brown hair, green jumper.
@Miss_Park = a kind kindergarten teacher in a cardigan.
@ben_drawing = Ben's crayon drawing of his dad as a giant.
@mia_drawing1 = Mia's crayon drawing of her family.
Each reference is one person or one object and appears once. No duplicates.

[VOICES]
@Ben VOICE: "A five-year-old boy, soft, shy, quick and quiet."
@Mia VOICE: "A five-year-old girl, high bright voice, bursting with eagerness, fast."
@Miss_Park VOICE: "A warm adult woman, calm, encouraging, gentle classroom pace."

[GOAL]
A five-shot, twenty-seven-second segment inside a two-minute animated comedy. Ben finishes his show-and-tell and Miss Park asks who is next. It ends the instant Mia's first line finishes — do not continue into her story, do not resolve anything, do not add an ending. The comedy is played completely straight. Nobody in frame knows anything is funny.

[CONTINUITY]
Location: the room in @classroom, morning, throughout. Never leave it.
The camera stays on the same side of the action as in @location1 for the whole segment and never crosses to the other side. @Mia is on the right-hand arc and this never flips.
Ten children and one teacher, deliberate diversity, zero face repeats.
Costume is fixed for the whole segment and never changes.

[SHOTS]
SHOT 1 | 0–3s
Wide on the carpet in @classroom: @Ben finishes holding up @ben_drawing; the class claps.
Hard cut.

SHOT 2 | 3–5s
Medium on @Mia, bouncing on her mat, hand already half up.
Hard cut.

SHOT 3 | 5–9s
Medium on @Miss_Park beside @Ben.
@Miss_Park: {Well done, Ben! That was great.}
@Ben: {Thank you, Miss Park.}
Hard cut.

SHOT 4 | 9–11s
Close on @Miss_Park turning to the class.
@Miss_Park: {Okay — so who's next?}
Hard cut.

SHOT 5 | 11–27s
Medium on @Mia shooting up off her mat, @mia_drawing1 clutched to her chest.
@Mia: {Me! Me Miss Park! I want to go next!}
Hard cut.

[VISUAL STYLE]
Feature-quality 3D animated film, production CG, not photorealistic and not flat cartoon. Warm morning daylight, soft subsurface glow through ears and skin, tactile materials. Depth of field as a natural in-camera optical artifact.

[CAMERA AND PERFORMANCE]
Five shots separated by four hard cuts. The body plays broad. The face stays honest. No mugging, no pulled faces, no comic reactions. Anticipation: every move winds the opposite way first. Snap and settle with overshoot on arrival. Moving holds: held poses breathe and micro-shift. Overlap and secondary action: hair, cloth and attachments arrive a beat late. Eye life: micro-saccades, live catchlights, realistic blinks.

[AUDIO]
Applause dying away, crayon scratching, small feet shuffling on carpet, quiet classroom room tone, subtle pizzicato strings.

[EXCLUSIONS]
The only spoken words in the entire segment are the lines in braces. Nothing else written anywhere in this prompt is dialogue, and nobody speaks who is not named on a line. No extra cuts anywhere. No unison movement. No subtitles, no watermark, no logo.

[MAINTAIN CONSISTENCY]
Ten children and one teacher: @Mia, @Ben and @Miss_Park bound to their references. Children are 4.5 heads tall (long torso, short legs); @Miss_Park is 7 heads tall.
